## Best Practices

### Signal Design
- Use descriptive signal names
- Pass immutable data or copies of mutable data
- Include error signals for exception handling
- Use typed signals when possible

### Slot Design
- Keep slots simple and fast
- Avoid blocking operations in slots
- Use slots for UI updates only
- Handle errors gracefully

### Thread Boundaries
- Never call UI methods from worker threads
- Always use signals for cross-thread communication
- Assume all shared data needs protection
- Design for thread safety from the beginning
